# .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# 🔴 The conceptual rule this file encodes:
#
#     Autonomous agents may REDUCE debt automatically.
#     Changing WHAT COUNTS AS ACCEPTABLE DEBT is a policy change and requires
#     human review.
#
# A ratchet baseline, a source-size waiver, a Biome lint severity, a Moon guard
# task and a CI guard step are all part of "what counts as acceptable debt".
# An agent that hits a guard failure can legitimately fix the code; it cannot
# legitimately redefine passing.
#
# Ownership is recorded against @snorreks — the repository's sole human
# maintainer and the only member of the BearlySleeping organization. No GitHub
# team exists for this repository (verified: `gh api orgs/BearlySleeping/teams`
# returns an empty list), so inventing `@BearlySleeping/platform` here would be
# an invalid owner that silently matches nothing. When a team is created, add it
# alongside the user rather than replacing them.
#
# ── Follow-up this file cannot perform ──
#
# CODEOWNERS is only advisory until branch protection requires it. The
# repository currently has no required status checks on `main`. To make the rule
# enforceable, a maintainer must, in repository settings:
#
#   1. require review from Code Owners on pull requests targeting `main`;
#   2. require the "Moon CI" check to pass before merging.
#
# Without (1) this file documents intent; with it, the intent is enforced.
#
# ── Machine-checked counterpart ──
#
# `scripts:guard-policy-diff` classifies every diff that touches these paths and
# prints `GUARD POLICY CHANGE` with a verdict (debt reduction / policy refactor /
# policy expansion). An unauthorized expansion fails CI. That check is the
# machine-readable half; CODEOWNERS is the human half.

# ── Guard policy: the definition of "passing" ──────────────────────────────

# This file itself: whoever can change who reviews guard policy can change guard
# policy. The registry lists `.github/CODEOWNERS` as a guard-policy path, so it
# is owned like one.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                      @snorreks

# Guard implementations and the shared ratchet framework.
/scripts/src/lib/ops/guard_*            @snorreks
/scripts/src/lib/ops/guards/            @snorreks

# Ratchet baselines and the source-size allowance files. A change here is
# either a debt reduction (allowed) or a policy expansion (needs review).
/scripts/src/lib/ops/*_baseline.json    @snorreks
/scripts/src/lib/ops/guard_source_file_size_exemptions.json @snorreks
/scripts/src/lib/ops/guard_source_file_size_waivers.json    @snorreks

# Lint severity and rule configuration.
/biome.json                             @snorreks

# Guard wiring: Moon tasks and CI.
/.moon/tasks/                           @snorreks
/.github/workflows/                     @snorreks

# The validation policy the contract pipeline obeys.
/scripts/src/lib/agents/contract_pipeline/validation_policy.ts @snorreks
/scripts/src/lib/agents/contract_pipeline/pre_push_gate.ts     @snorreks

# ── Data-plane and security invariants ────────────────────────────────────

# The server data plane is a hard architectural invariant.
/packages/backend/database/             @snorreks
/apps/frontend/hub/src/lib/server/      @snorreks

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/bun.lock                               @snorreks
